---
import ProjectDetail from '../../layouts/ProjectDetail.astro';

const demoVideo = '/videos/galaxy-zoo-demo.mp4';
---

<ProjectDetail
  title="Galaxy Zoo: Galaxy Morphology Classifier"
  description="Trained an image classifier on Galaxy Zoo 2 telescope images to sort galaxies into spiral, barred spiral, elliptical and merger."
  tags={['Computer Vision', 'Vertex AI', 'AutoML', 'Astronomy', 'Google Cloud']}
  demoVideo={demoVideo}
>
  <section class="project-grid">
    <article class="project-card summary-card">
      <h2>What it does</h2>
      <p>
        Given a photo of a galaxy from the Sloan Digital Sky Survey, the model predicts its shape. The labels come from citizen-science volunteer votes, converted into clean classes with the published Hart et al. 2016 debiased classification table.
      </p>
      <div class="summary-list">
        <div>
          <strong>Data</strong>
          <p>239,030 labeled images from Galaxy Zoo 2: 96,458 elliptical, 95,111 spiral, 45,303 barred spiral and 2,158 merger.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Model</strong>
          <p>Vertex AI AutoML Vision, with the architecture chosen by AutoML's own search rather than hand-designed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="project-card detail-card">
      <h2>Results (test split)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>AUC-PR 0.857, log loss 0.263.</li>
        <li>At the 0.5 threshold: 80% precision and 75% recall.</li>
        <li>About 78% overall accuracy, computed from the confusion matrix.</li>
        <li>Per class: elliptical 92%, spiral 70%, barred spiral 67%, merger 0%.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="project-section">
    <div class="section-content">
      <h2>How it was built</h2>

      <div class="section-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Data preparation</h3>
          <p>
            Downloaded and extracted 243,434 images, then joined them to the label table. The 239,030 that remained after dropping unclassifiable ones were used.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Labeling rule</h3>
          <p>
            The merger flag wins first, then <code>SB</code> becomes barred spiral, <code>S</code> spiral and <code>E</code> elliptical.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Sanity checks</h3>
          <p>
            The pipeline stops if the join looks broken: too few images, too few classes, or a class with fewer than 500 examples.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Training</h3>
          <p>
            Uploaded everything to Cloud Storage, created a Vertex AI image dataset, and trained with Vertex AI AutoML Vision. The split was 80/10/10, with an 80 node-hour budget and early stopping disabled.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="project-section project-usage">
    <h2>Honest limitation</h2>
    <p>
      Mergers are under 1% of the data, and the model never learned to predict them. This is a class imbalance problem. The next step would be class weighting, oversampling, or collecting more merger examples.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProjectDetail>
